  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "A fair amount of VRChat players have weird looking characters in their nameplate. This does provide an aesthetic change, but it makes finding their username on VRChat.com or in the social menu extremely hard. If they are toxic/crashers/racists I can block them in-game at once, but I can't search their name because of the weird characters! I think it should be priority for names to be easily searchable and findable to prevent issues like these. This also goes along with invisible characters. I propose that VRChat names should only include characters that are easily typeable and don't include any \"edgy\" characters.",
